    {
      "marker": "8",
      "text": "8. Students must declare and complete a minor in either (1) a foreign language (in the Department of Languages, Literatures and Cultures) or (2) a minor in an area studies program from the following list: a. African Studies b. Asian Studies c. European Studies d. Islamic World Studies e. Latin American, Caribbean, and US Latinx Studies f. Middle East Studies g. Slavic, East-Central European, and Eurasian Studies Note: Courses applied toward general education requirements cannot be counted toward the minor. No course may satisfy both major and minor requirements. All minor courses must be passed with a grade of C or higher. At least half of the courses in the minor must be completed in residence at the University. Students can satisfy this requirement by completing a second major.",
